WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.460
Two independent checks now meet.
Evaluation gave h of one P,

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:09.960
h of negative one P, and h of i
P, each with norm four u squared.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:15.520
Separately, the parity check showed that
their coefficients can be divided by two.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:17.480
One result supplies the norm;

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:21.280
the other justifies exact
division in the coefficient rings.

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:26.550
Define c of P as h of
one P divided by two,

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.220
d of P as h of negative
one P divided by two,

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:33.750
and g of P as h of i P divided by two.

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:36.560
The coefficients of c and d are integers.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:39.480
Those of g are Gaussian integers.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:44.580
All three retain the relation
P to the u squared equals one.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:47.430
Star fixes the real number two.

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:52.520
So dividing h of one P by two
also divides its star by two.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:56.160
In c times c star, one half
appears in each factor.

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:00.960
The two halves multiply to one
quarter. Substitute the original norm,

00:01:01.233 --> 00:01:06.540
four u squared, then cancel
four. The result is u squared.

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:11.100
The same calculation applies to d and g.

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:14.700
All three normalized
polynomials have product

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:17.967
with their star equal to u squared. For g,

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:22.620
star conjugates the Gaussian
coefficients as well as reversing powers.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:26.420
The real scalar two stays
fixed under that operation.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:32.140
In our guiding case u equals three,
the original norm is thirty six.

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:35.570
Dividing each factor by two
divides their product by four.

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:38.650
Thirty six divided by four is nine.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:41.600
Now choose an allowed input zeta,

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:44.380
satisfying zeta to the
u squared equals one.

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:49.460
At these roots of unity, star becomes
complex conjugation. Each normalized

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:53.460
norm identity therefore gives an output
times its conjugate equal to u squared.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:58.340
Its squared absolute value is u
squared, so its absolute value is u.

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:03.540
When u is three, send an allowed
ninth root through c, d, and g.

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:06.490
Their three outputs lie on
the circle of radius three.

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:10.420
Keep this output circle separate
from the unit circle of input roots.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:14.880
The angles in our drawing are schematic:
the argument fixes their lengths,

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:17.140
while later nodes compare their phases.
